  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nMarkets showing cautious optimism in pre-market with SPY up 0.26% to $741.17, though NASDAQ lagging slightly at -0.04%. VIX dropping to 24.48 signals some risk appetite returning, while small caps (IWM) leading with +1.32% suggests rotation into domestic plays. Geopolitical relief from Iran-Israel ceasefire driving early sentiment.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>NFIB Business Optimism (10:00 AM)</strong> - Small business sentiment will be key given IWM strength</li>\n<li><strong>ADP Employment Weekly (12:15 PM)</strong> - Labor market data ahead of Friday's NFP</li>\n<li><strong>Trade Balance (12:30 PM)</strong> - Import/export data amid ongoing trade tensions</li>\n<li><strong>Energy sector weakness</strong> - XLE down 1.85% despite Middle East tensions easing</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>Small cap leadership suggests confidence in domestic economy. Real estate (XLRE) up 2.07% indicates rate cut expectations building momentum.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Iran-Israel ceasefire removing major geopolitical overhang. Oil complex cooling off as supply disruption fears fade.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nClear defensive-to-cyclical rotation underway with Real Estate, Consumer Discretionary, and Financials leading while Tech and Energy lag. XLF up 1.21% suggests market pricing in economic resilience despite rate uncertainty. Energy's 1.85% drop counterintuitive given recent tensions - watch for oversold bounce if geopolitics heat up again.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Tech weakness (XLK -0.55%) could drag NASDAQ lower. VIX still elevated at 24+ suggests underlying nervousness beneath surface optimism.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY 742</strong> - Pre-market high; break above opens path to 745 resistance</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ 710</strong> - Critical support; losing this level targets 705</li>\n<li><strong>VIX 25</strong> - Holding below keeps risk-on trade alive</li>\n<li><strong>XLE 78</strong> - Energy oversold bounce level if geopolitics flare</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>",
